!Dialogue
|- class="article-row-main"
|Interaction 1 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Oh you came back!}}
|-
|Interaction 2 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: For a moment I thought you wouldn't}}
|-
|Interaction 3 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I'm sorry if I spooked you a little bit last time}}
|-
|Interaction 4 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Sometimes I get carried away too much and tell personal stories}}
|-
|Interaction 5 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I apologize}}
|-
|Interaction 6 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: You can call me Tal, some people call me TK}}
|-
|Interaction 7 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I don't actually live there, I'm just visiting}}
|-
|Interaction 8 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe one day I’ll show you my place}}
|-
|Interaction 9 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I think I had dwarves somewhere in my family tree}}
|-
|Interaction 10 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: That's why I look like one}}
|-
|Interaction 11 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I like visiting islands, some more than others}}
|-
|Interaction 12 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Golden Mines, Crimson Isle... haven't been there in ages}}
|-
|Interaction 13 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I used to go to the End a lot, not anymore}}
|-
|Interaction 14 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The dragon heart corrupts everything, even the people}}
|-
|Interaction 15 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I like it better down here, there are people like you}}
|-
|Interaction 16 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The story of these mines is old, older than the End island for sure!}}
|-
|Interaction 17 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: You do know the story of the End island right?}}
|-
|Interaction 18 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Hum, well that's awkward}}
|-
|Interaction 19 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I guess they don't really teach you much do they}}
|-
|Interaction 20 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Unfortunately I don't know enough details myself}}
|-
|Interaction 21 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I do know a few things, you remember the giant skeleton on the island nearby?}}
|-
|Interaction 22 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The heart of that creature is sealed on the End island}}
|-
|Interaction 23 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Not many people are left, who can tell the story of that day}}
|-
|Interaction 24 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe Jerry saw it, when he was very young}}
|-
|Interaction 25 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: And even he was probably born much later}}
|-
|Interaction 26 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The Calamity is the reason why the earth got shattered into many islands}}
|-
|Interaction 27 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I wish I knew more, it's a fantastic subject}}
|-
|Interaction 28 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The end of an era, and the beginning of a much darker one}}
|-
|Interaction 29 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Sorry if I'm boring you, I like history}}
|-
|Interaction 30 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I went to the Sky Academy, greater teachers there}}
|-
|Interaction 31 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: You should go there someday, even greater adventurers need to learn a few things!}}
|-
|Interaction 32 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: My parents always told me to focus on my studies}}
|-
|Interaction 33 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: They were right, I'm a successful young man now!}}
|-
|Interaction 34 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe not so young, but my point still stands}}
|-
|Interaction 35 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Studies on one side and fun on the other, both are very important}}
|-
|Interaction 36 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Yin and yang, one should not go without the other}}
|-
|Interaction 37 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The Academy was tough, but I met a few friends there}}
|-
|Interaction 38 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: You know the banker?}}
|-
|Interaction 39 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: He was in my promotion back then}}
|-
|Interaction 40 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: He invented the bank!}}
|-
|Interaction 41 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I still have no idea where all that interest is coming from}}
|-
|Interaction 42 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: A genius this guy}}
|-
|Interaction 43 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I like seeing the world evolve through time}}
|-
|Interaction 44 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: What they did to the village a few years ago was great}}
|-
|Interaction 45 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I feel like we entered the modern age}}
|-
|Interaction 46 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The technology is progressing fast, who knows what's coming next!}}
|-
|Interaction 47 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I'm sure one day people will fly to the moon}}
|-
|Interaction 48 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I knew a time without adventurers, without banks and auctions}}
|-
|Interaction 49 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Not much was happening back then}}
|-
|Interaction 50 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: And then it happened}}
|-
|Interaction 51 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: One day hordes of people appeared out of nowhere}}
|-
|Interaction 52 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Nobody seems to know why}}
|-
|Interaction 53 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I have my theory but I won't tell you}}
|-
|Interaction 54 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: You would think I'm crazy, maybe you already do}}
|-
|Interaction 55 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: All those people at once}}
|-
|Interaction 56 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: It was really overwhelming}}
|-
|Interaction 57 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: It did create so many business opportunities}}
|-
|Interaction 58 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The economy is booming}}
|-
|Interaction 59 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: That guy, Bazaar, he really took advantage of it}}
|-
|Interaction 60 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Bazaar isn't even his real name}}
|-
|Interaction 61 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: He changed his name to Bazaar because it was better for business, he said}}
|-
|Interaction 62 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: A real specimen}}
|-
|Interaction 63 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Lots of people think they understand the market}}
|-
|Interaction 64 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I gave up on it}}
|-
|Interaction 65 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I did buy some stocks of stonks when he opened}}
|-
|Interaction 66 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I still have a few}}
|-
|Interaction 67 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: That Warren guy made a lot of money and disappeared}}
|-
|Interaction 68 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Another shark}}
|-
|Interaction 69 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe I should sell my own currency and make people believe it's worth many coins}}
|-
|Interaction 70 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Like Talcoins?}}
|-
|Interaction 71 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The value of anything is in the eyes of the buyers}}
|-
|Interaction 72 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I'm sure I could raise the price of anything if I really tried}}
|-
|Interaction 73 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Some people do that all the time in the community}}
|-
|Interaction 74 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I like it though, it creates opportunities for everyone}}
|-
|Interaction 75 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I think a lot of what happens around here can serve as a life lesson}}
|-
|Interaction 76 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: It's important to experience the right things when you are young}}
|-
|Interaction 77 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Even bad moments can be blessings in disguise}}
|-
|Interaction 78 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Someone scammed me a very valuable thing one day}}
|-
|Interaction 79 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: They even got away with it, awful}}
|-
|Interaction 80 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: But never again have I gotten fooled}}
|-
|Interaction 81 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: If I could I would pay him double}}
|-
|Interaction 82 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: A lesson for a few coins, a great deal}}
|-
|Interaction 83 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Always stay vigilant}}
|-
|Interaction 84 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Some people don't see it the same way}}
|-
|Interaction 85 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Do you know the origin of the word utopia?}}
|-
|Interaction 86 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: It means a place that does not exist}}
|-
|Interaction 87 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Even the people who created the word knew it was a paradox}}
|-
|Interaction 88 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Some people are smarter than hundreds of other combined}}
|-
|Interaction 89 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Do you think they were born that way, or became?}}
|-
|Interaction 90 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I have my own view on the matter}}
|-
|Interaction 91 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: My opinion is that it's a little bit of both}}
|-
|Interaction 92 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The smartest baby would become a monkey if it wasn't taught anything}}
|-
|Interaction 93 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Someone told me a story one day}}
|-
|Interaction 94 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Bird eggs are grey and dirty, snake eggs are white and clean}}
|-
|Interaction 95 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The bird decided to sit on the clean egg instead of his}}
|-
|Interaction 96 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: The egg hatched and the snake ate the bird}}
|-
|Interaction 97 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: He told me the moral of the story is that birds are stupid}}
|-
|Interaction 98 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: But is that the moral of the story?}}
|-
|Interaction 99 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe it's about appearances being deceiving}}
|-
|Interaction 100 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: A clean shell can hide a dirty mind}}
|-
|Interaction 101 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe it's about beauty being subjective}}
|-
|Interaction 102 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: If the bird found dirty eggs pretty, he wouldn't have gotten in that situation}}
|-
|Interaction 103 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe it's about planning ahead}}
|-
|Interaction 104 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Short term comfort can lead to troubles in the future}}
|-
|Interaction 105 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: Maybe it's about trusting your family more than others}}
|-
|Interaction 106 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: If you tell the same story to multiple people they might understand it differently}}
|-
|Interaction 107 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: What do you think is the moral of the story?}}
|-
|Interaction 108 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I love talking, but I also think a lot!}}
|-
|Interaction 109 After Returning
| style="text-align: left;" |{{Dialogue|&e[NPC] Tal Ker&f: I'm going to think for a bit, thanks for listening to me! See you!}}
|}
